{"step_index":852,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T18:21:01Z","content":"I have updated the application configuration and file ingestion pipeline to handle files larger than 200 MB:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Web Uploader Limit Increased to 1 GB\nStreamlit's default file upload limit (200 MB) has been increased to **1,024 MB (1 GB)** via [`.streamlit/config.toml`](file:///C:/Users/win-10/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/neurax_app/.streamlit/config.toml):\n- You can now drag and drop your >200 MB `.xlsx` or `.csv` file directly into the **Model 3** tab uploader in the sidebar without rejection.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Instant Local File Path Ingestion (Recommended for Large Files)\nTo avoid waiting for large files to upload through the browser, you can also load directly from disk:\n1. In the sidebar, expand **\"Telemetry Datasets\"** $\\rightarrow$ select the **\"Model 3\"** tab.\n2. Open the **\"Or enter local file path\"** dropdown.\n3. Verify or paste the path to your file (e.g., `D:\\acceleration\\Model_3.xlsx` or `D:\\acceleration\\Model_3.csv`).\n4. Click **\"Load from Disk\"** for instant loading.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Memory & Speed Optimizations\n- **Chunked Sampling**: Large datasets (>20 MB / 600,000+ rows) are automatically parsed in high-efficiency sampled chunks, preventing RAM exhaustion or browser freezes."}
